From 5038043d8fa1d7231b0e937b9ed651e4d9c8f4e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:29:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(tools,ui): built-in BT30/BT40/CAT40 holder library
 (ER and Weldon)

A built-in holder library (camcraft-tools::holder_library): BT30 and
BT40 (JIS B 6339 / MAS 403) and CAT40 (ASME B5.50) tapers, each as an
ER collet chuck (ER16-ER32; ISO 15488 / DIN 6499) or a Weldon side-lock
holder (DIN 1835 B / DIN 6359 bores), drawn as spun profiles: nut or
body, flange as a full cylinder, standoff, closed at the gauge line.

SetToolBody::library drops an entry into a tool's holder as one
undoable command over SetToolBody::spun (gauge length and projection
adjustable), so it lands editable and is judged by the existing body
path. The tool editor's Profile tab gets a Library holder picker with a
gauge length field and Apply holder. Dimensions and the small-BT
decision are recorded in docs/decisions/793-taper-holders.md; the MCP
tool is #799.

Fixes #793

